{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966995,"nonce":"mdyU9d9aEpUn6yU61DSwEZmXfE0=","title":"No AOT pipeline or standalone CLI for shipping a DSL app","message":"JIT covers desktop development. Shipping does not:\n\n- iOS forbids JIT, so an AOT path is the only way a `.blinc` program\n  reaches the platform at all. Android is AOT-only for the same\n  packaging reasons.\n- `blinc_dsl_codegen` is planned and absent: the LLVM AOT pipeline would\n  emit objects and package them as a static library to link, mobile, or\n  an executable, desktop.\n- `blinc_cli` would grow `init`, `dev` and `build --target`, bundling\n  LLVM and per-platform prebuilt archives so someone without cargo can\n  build. Roughly what `flutter build` does.\n- wasm AOT is deferred behind Zyntax's own story for it.\n\nDetail lives in the DSL section of the root ROADMAP.md.","files":null}]}